  q(SYS,'Which nursing action is important for a patient with hemophilia?','Avoid IM injections and apply pressure to puncture sites',['Give aspirin for joint pain','Encourage contact sports','Massage swollen joints firmly to reduce bleeding'],'C','Patients with hemophilia lack clotting factors, so even minor injuries can cause serious bleeding.',PP),
  q(SYS,'A patient with dysphagia after a stroke is eating. Which technique lowers the risk of aspiration?','Sit upright and tuck the chin when swallowing',['Lie flat while eating','Drink thin liquids through a straw','Tilt the head back when swallowing'],'D','Thickened liquids and small bites are also used, as ordered by the speech therapist.',PP),
  q(SYS,'When should a patient with cystic fibrosis take pancreatic enzyme capsules?','With every meal and snack',['Only at bedtime','Once a week','Only when stools are formed'],'A','The enzymes help digest fat and protein; without them, stools are bulky and greasy and weight drops.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which device is used at night to treat obstructive sleep apnea?','A CPAP machine',['A nasal cannula at 2 L/min','An incentive spirometer','A peak flow meter used each morning'],'B','CPAP gives steady air pressure that keeps the upper airway open during sleep.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which teaching is correct for a patient taking rifampin for tuberculosis?','Urine, sweat and tears may turn orange-red',['Stop the drug when you feel better','Take it only when you cough','Expect your skin to turn blue'],'C','Rifampin harmlessly colors body fluids, but it can stain soft contact lenses.',PP),
  q(SYS,'How is hepatitis A most often spread?','By the fecal-oral route, such as contaminated food or water',['By sharing needles','Through blood transfusions','Only through blood, such as shared needles or transfusions'],'D','Good handwashing and the hepatitis A vaccine help prevent spread of this infection.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Why is a patient with a new ileostomy at higher risk for dehydration?','The output is liquid and contains a lot of water and electrolytes',['The stoma absorbs water','The large intestine works harder','The small intestine stops absorbing any nutrients after surgery'],'A','Because the colon is bypassed, less water is absorbed, so patients need extra fluids.',PP),
  q(SYS,'After a liver biopsy, how should the patient be positioned?','On the right side to put pressure on the site',['On the left side','Sitting upright in a chair','Prone with the legs elevated on pillows'],'B','Lying on the right side presses on the puncture site and lowers the risk of bleeding.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which exercise helps a patient with stress urinary incontinence?','Kegel (pelvic floor) exercises',['Sit-ups','Running','Limiting fluids to 500 mL a day so the bladder fills more slowly'],'C','Kegel exercises strengthen the pelvic floor, which helps control leakage with coughing or laughing.',PP),
  q(SYS,'A child has dark, tea-colored urine and puffy eyes a few weeks after strep throat. What is suspected?','Acute glomerulonephritis',['Kidney stones','Bladder infection','Nephrotic syndrome without any blood in the urine'],'D','Glomerulonephritis is an immune reaction that damages the kidney filters after a strep infection.',PP),
  q(SYS,'How often should males be taught to perform testicular self-examination?','Monthly, after a warm shower',['Once a year','Only if pain occurs','Only during a yearly physical exam done by a health care provider'],'A','Testicular cancer is most common in young men, and a painless lump is a common first sign.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which symptoms are classic signs of high blood glucose?','Increased thirst and urination',['Sweating and shakiness','Cold, clammy skin','Rapid weight gain with swelling of the feet'],'B','Polydipsia, polyuria and polyphagia are the classic signs of hyperglycemia.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which finding is typical of systemic lupus erythematosus?','A butterfly-shaped rash across the cheeks and nose',['A ring-shaped rash','Silvery scales on the elbows','A painful rash in a band on one side'],'C','Lupus is an autoimmune disease, and patients should protect their skin from the sun.',PP),
  q(SYS,'A patient with a femur fracture develops confusion, shortness of breath and petechiae on the chest. What is suspected?','Fat embolism',['Compartment syndrome','Osteomyelitis','Delirium from pain medicine'],'D','Fat embolism usually occurs within 72 hours after a long-bone fracture and is an emergency.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which action is correct for a patient in skeletal traction?','Keep the weights hanging freely',['Rest the weights on the floor','Remove the weights for meals','Lift the weights when repositioning'],'A','Weights must hang freely to keep a steady pull and correct alignment of the bone.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Pain that radiates from the lower back down the back of one leg is called:','Sciatica',['Carpal tunnel syndrome','Plantar fasciitis','Shin splints'],'B','Sciatica often results from a herniated disc pressing on the sciatic nerve roots.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which teaching is important for a patient with Bell palsy?','Protect the eye on the affected side',['Avoid all chewing','Stay in bed','Keep the eye on that side uncovered and open at night'],'C','The eyelid may not close fully, so eye drops and a patch at night help prevent corneal damage.',PP),
  q(SYS,'A patient has a seizure that lasts longer than 5 minutes. Which drug is commonly given first?','IV lorazepam',['Oral phenytoin','Acetaminophen','Insulin'],'D','A seizure lasting over 5 minutes is status epilepticus, a medical emergency that needs fast treatment.',PP),
  q(SYS,'After a lumbar puncture, what helps prevent a spinal headache?','Lying flat and drinking fluids as ordered',['Placing a heating pad on the back','Limiting fluids','Sitting upright and walking right away to keep fluid moving'],'A','Keeping the patient flat for a time and giving fluids help replace spinal fluid lost from the puncture.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which symptom is typical of macular degeneration?','Loss of central vision',['Loss of side vision first','Severe eye pain','Itchy, red eyes'],'B','Macular degeneration damages the center of the retina, so reading and recognizing faces become hard.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Using the rule of nines, what percentage of body surface is one entire adult arm?','9 percent',['18 percent','1 percent','36 percent'],'C','In adults each arm is 9 percent, each leg is 18 percent and the front of the trunk is 18 percent.',PP),
  q(SYS,'In the ABCDE guide for melanoma, what does the “E” stand for?','Evolving, or changing over time',['Elevation only','Even color','Edges that are smooth'],'D','A mole that changes in size, shape or color should be checked promptly by a provider.',PP),
  q(SYS,'Which teaching is important for a patient taking lithium?','Keep sodium and fluid intake steady',['Cut out all salt','Drink very little water','Take it only when feeling down'],'A','Low sodium or dehydration raises lithium levels and can cause toxicity, with tremor and vomiting.',PP),
  q(SYS,'A patient who drinks heavily is admitted. About 6 to 48 hours later, tremors and sweating begin. What is happening?','Alcohol withdrawal',['Hypothermia','A stroke','An allergic reaction'],'B','Withdrawal can progress to seizures and delirium tremens, so the nurse monitors closely.',PP)
